-- title:
--   Places of ℚ̄(X₀(q)) determined by values over a number field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. a number field inside a fixed algebraic closure. Write $F$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathsf{q}))/\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained by adjoining to $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)` (itself the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((\mathsf{q}))$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $1\cdot q$). Let $W_1, W_2$ be places of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, each given by a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, distinct from the whole field and a principal ideal ring. Assume that for every $g \in F$ whose underlying Laurent series lies in `fieldOver (1 * q) K`, the subfield of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathsf{q}))$ generated by the constant series of the elements of $K$ together with the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $1\cdot q$, and for every $c_0 \in \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, one has $W_1$ takes the value $c_0$ at $g$ if and only if $W_2$ does; here a place takes the value $c_0$ at $g$ when $g$ lies in its valuation subring and the residue of $g$ is the image of $c_0$ in the residue field. Then $W_1 = W_2$.
--
--   This is the constant-field-extension step for the modular function field: a place of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(q))$ is pinned down by its values on the functions whose $\mathsf{q}$-expansions have coefficients in a number field $K$, the pair $(j, j_q)$ generating the field over $K$. It is used in the node-descent analysis to prove existence and uniqueness of the places of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(q))$ centred at the supersingular-type points with $j = 0$ and $j = 1728$, and it relies on the fact that every place of this field has residue degree one over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_place_eq_of_forall_hasValue_iff_of_mem_fieldOver.lean

